 "modules": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "EDITING & STRUCTURE\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 81 to 96\n   1 Number of main characters\n   2 Groups in the hour\n   3 Exit\n   4 How often a main is in the season\n   5 Scene change rate\n   6 Sequence lengths\n   7 How a scene begins\n   8 How scenes join (storytelling)\n   9 Call and response\n  10 Repetition scheme\n  11 Signature image or line\n  12 Contrast map\n  13 Tension\n  14 Energy\n  15 Visual density\n  16 Constant\nCV-CC 2: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 6, CC 97 to 112\n   1 Psych-out shift\n   2 Clipped or flowing cuts\n   3 Human touch in camera and cuts\n   4 Motif shape\n   5 Cross-cutting\n   6 When the audience learns it\n   7 Story point of view\n   8 Scene length\n   9 How the scene ends\n  10 The opening grab\n  11 Ends where it starts\n  12 Multicam angle switching\n  13 Nested scene\n  14 Time and speed\n  15 Shots in order\n  16 The story told backwards\nCV-CC 3: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 7, CC 1 to 16\n   1 A glimpse of what is coming\n   2 The same moment from another side\n   3 It seems to end, but doesn't\n   4 Someone telling the story\n   5 How far apart the surprises come\n   6 The promise of the opening\n   7 A stretch where nothing pulls\n   8 Leaving at the best part\n   9 Where the audience stands in the telling\n  10 The order the story is told in\n  11 A story told inside a story\n  12 Seeing others through their own life\n  13 How we learn what happened before\n  14 A glimpse of someone's whole life\n  15 suite: Two-person hour\n  16 suite: Build\nCV-CC 4: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 7, CC 17 to 32\n   1 suite: Drop\n   2 suite: Signature return\n   3 suite: Crime, Tarantino style\n   4 suite: Horror\n   5 suite: Action\n   6 suite: Western\n   7 suite: Musical\n   8 suite: Documentary look (camera and light)\n   9 suite: Surrealist\n  10 suite: Romantic comedy\n  11 suite: Viral short: hook and loop\n  12 suite: Episode cliffhanger\n  13 suite: Stop-motion feel\n  14 suite: The big moment\n  15 suite: Breakneck pace\n  16 suite: Slow and patient\nCV-CC 5: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 7, CC 33 to 48\n   1 suite: Cut like music\n   2 suite: Ensemble patchwork\n   3 suite: Losing a main character\n   4 suite: Studio sitcom\n   5 suite: A story inside the story\n   6 suite: From the end, back\n   7 suite: How did I get here?\n   8 suite: The same night, twice\n   9 suite: It is not over\n  10 suite: Just one more episode\n  11 suite: A promise kept\n  12 suite: Waking up a flat middle\n  13 suite: Trust me (don't)\n  14 suite: We know everything\n  15 suite: A tale by the fire\n  16 suite: Long talk that snaps into violence\nCV-CC 6: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 7, CC 49 to 64\n   1 pair: When tension peaks, a long silence\n   2 pair: When energy drops, the hold is long\n   3 pair: When suite Build, suite Drop\n   4 pair: When suite Aggressive camera, suite Quiet confession\n   5 pair: When suite Storm, suite Breathing room\n   6 pair: When time slows, the bits in the air hang\n   7 pair: When scenes start changing faster, the tension climbs\n   8 pair: When tension climbs, scenes get shorter\n   9 pair: When the hour splits into two groups, the film cuts back and forth between them\n  10 pair: When the film cuts between two places faster and faster, the clock feels tighter\n  11 pair: When a scene starts in the middle of the action, the audience starts asking questions\n  12 pair: When every shot answers the one before, laughs come faster\n  13 pair: When shots come in threes, the third one becomes the punchline\n  14 pair: When the same moment keeps repeating, it turns into a running gag\n  15 pair: When the film's signature image comes back, the old feeling comes back with it\n  16 pair: When scenes are built to clash, the feeling flips at the cut\nCV-CC 7: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 7, CC 65 to 80\n   1 pair: When one sound or image is held under everything, dread builds\n   2 pair: When a scare turns out to be fake, the audience laughs with relief\n   3 pair: When the cuts get louder and sharper, the energy jumps\n   4 pair: When the camera feels like a nosy person in the room, awkward moments get more awkward\n   5 pair: When a repeating tune or image keeps climbing, hope climbs with it\n   6 pair: When the story hops between characters, the audience learns things before they do\n   7 pair: When a main character shows up more often, their own story gets heavier\n   8 pair: When more main characters share the spotlight, their stories start crossing\n   9 pair: When a main character dies, the tears come soon after\n  10 pair: When a scene plays out inside another scene, the audience starts doubting what's real\n  11 pair: When the shots get short, the energy climbs\n  12 pair: When the story runs backwards, we already know how it ends\n  13 pair: When the story runs backwards, we ask why\n  14 pair: When the glimpse of the future shows a death, dread rises\n  15 pair: When the glimpse of the future is clearer, the ending feels fixed\n  16 pair: When the second look changes more, we know more than they do\nCV-CC 8: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 7, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When the second look changes everything, the story flips\n   2 pair: When the fake ending is more convincing, we let our breath out\n   3 pair: When the villain comes back after the ending, things get worse\n   4 pair: When the teller is lying, we cannot trust what we see\n   5 pair: When the story is told to a child, tenderness grows\n   6 pair: When surprises come more often, tension rises\n   7 pair: When the opening grabs with a promise, the promise gets clearer\n   8 pair: When the opening's promise is broken, the film turns on us\n   9 pair: When nothing pulls, the audience drifts\n  10 pair: When a flat stretch is fixed with a clock, the clock starts running\n  11 pair: When a flat stretch is fixed with a question, someone asks it out loud\n  12 pair: When a scene ends on a cliffhanger, we leave at the best part\n  13 pair: When the film cuts between stories more, it leaves each nearer its peak\n  14 pair: When we leave a story at its peak, its question rides along\n  15 pair: When we are let into one head, the voice-over grows\n  16 pair: When the telling talks to us, the character looks at the lens\nCV-CC 9: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 7, CC 97 to 112\n   1 pair: When we know more than the hero, suspense builds\n   2 pair: When the telling can't be trusted, we see the moment again\n   3 pair: When the teller is lying, said and meant pull apart\n   4 pair: When time jumps more, memories lie over the present\n   5 pair: When the story starts at the end, glimpses of it return\n   6 pair: When the frame is a diary, words are read out loud\n   7 pair: When the past is shown, not told, we hold more back\n   8 pair: When a stranger's life echoes the hero's, the theme sharpens\n   9 pair: When we glimpse a whole life, a road not taken appears\n  10 pair: When the hero's life falls, they see the worst in others\n  11 pair: When the view is colored more, the telling can't be trusted\n  12 pair: When the talk runs long and casual, violence arrives without warning\n  13 pair: When a chapter card appears, the story jumps to someone else's side\n  14 pair: When a false scare passes, the real one comes right after\n  15 pair: When the cutting jumps between the crew, the tension climbs\n  16 pair: When the film notices it has gone too far, it just stops and moves on\nCV-CC 10: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 8, CC 1 to 10\n   1 pair: When the cut goes to whoever is listening, the joke lands twice\n   2 pair: When violence breaks out, the next scene is calm and ordinary\n   3 pairs: Long-form shape\n   4 pairs: The squeeze\n   5 pairs: We know how it ends\n   6 pairs: Leaving at the peak\n   7 pairs: Waking the middle\n   8 pairs: The telling turns\n   9 pairs: Time out of order\n  10 pairs: Long talk that snaps into violence: the moves"
   },
